 march to Shiloh","width":1600,"height":1200,"loading":"lazy"}]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Lew Wallace’s delayed march"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Wallace chose the Shunpike toward Sherman’s original right, learned after 2 p.m. that the army had fallen back, countermarched, crossed to the River Road, and struggled through the Snake Creek bottomland."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"map-actions","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/shiloh-lew-wallace-march.svg","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Open full-size map ","$L15"]}],"$L16"]}],"$undefined"]}]]}],"$L17"]}]
10:["$","section",null,{"className":"reference-section","id":"events","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What happened"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"timeline factual-timeline","children":[["$","div","The episode places the Hornet’s Nest in context",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":42,"label":"0:42"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"The episode places the Hornet’s Nest in context"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The center’s defense was important, but it did not face the same concentration of Confederate forces as Sherman and McClernand on the western battlefield."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Sherman and McClernand reorganized at Jones Field",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":233,"label":"3:53"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Sherman and McClernand reorganized at Jones Field"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Seven brigades had suffered different levels of damage; only McDowell’s brigade remained fresh and nearly intact."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Sherman decided to counterattack",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":367,"label":"6:07"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Sherman decided to counterattack"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"He judged that Confederate disorganization created an opportunity to delay the next assault and restore part of the United States position."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Fourteen regiments moved south",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":470,"label":"7:50"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Fourteen regiments moved south"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Around noon or 12:30, a ragged line advanced from Jones Field. About one-third of the formations in the sector did not participate."}]]}]]}],["$","div","The counterattack achieved surprise",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":530,"label":"8:50"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"The counterattack achieved surprise"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"McDowell’s and Marsh’s brigades formed the most stable parts of the advance and collected soldiers separated from other units."}]]}]]}],["$","div","The fighting divided into two results",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":587,"label":"9:47"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"The fighting divided into two results"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Marsh fought a bloody standoff against Preston Smith and Patton Anderson, while McDowell drove Confederates back nearly half a mile."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Hardee threatened McDowell’s exposed flank",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":615,"label":"10:15"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Hardee threatened McDowell’s exposed flank"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The flank threat halted further progress, and ammunition shortages then forced United States regiments back to Jones Field."}]]}]]}],["$","div","The counterattack delayed the Confederate left",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":664,"label":"11:04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"The counterattack delayed the Confederate left"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"It increased the confusion among Hardee’s intermingled formations and postponed another organized offensive."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Grant expected two reinforcing divisions",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":748,"label":"12:28"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Grant expected two reinforcing divisions"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"William Nelson approached on the east bank from Savannah, while Lew Wallace’s 3rd Division was near Crump’s Landing on the west bank."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Nelson’s march was delayed by mud",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"seconds":810,"label":"13:30"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Nelson’s march was delayed by mud"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The head of his column did not reach the river opposite Pittsburg Landing until nearly sunset, too late for Sunday’s main fighting."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Wallace assembled at Stoney Lonesome",{"className":"moment","children":["$L19","$L1a"]}],"$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26"]}]]}]
11:["$","section",null,{"className":"reference-section","id":"people","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"People and command"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"command-grid reference-command","children":[["$","section","United States",{"className":"command-column #315f8c","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"United States"}],[["$","div","Army of the Tennessee",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army of the Tennessee"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Ulysses S. Grant"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Directed Wallace to march and sent multiple staff officers to find and accelerate the 3rd Division"}]]}],["$","div","5th Division",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"5th Division"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"William T. Sherman"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Organized the Jones Field counterattack with McClernand"}]]}],["$","div","1st Division",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"1st Division"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"John A. McClernand"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Sent staff through the disorganized regiments and advanced beside Sherman"}]]}],["$","div","Principal counterattack brigades",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Principal counterattack brigades"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"John McDowell / C. C. Marsh"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"McDowell on the right; Marsh in the center; rallied elements joined both"}]]}],["$","div","3rd Division",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"3rd Division"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Lew Wallace"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Three brigades marching from Stoney Lonesome to Pittsburg Landing"}]]}],["$","div","Grant’s staff",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Grant’s staff"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"John A. Rawlins / James B. McPherson / William R. Rowley"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Located Wallace, clarified the route, and urged the division forward"}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Confederacy",{"className":"command-column #9a3d32","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Confederacy"}],[["$","div","Confederate left",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Confederate left"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"William J. Hardee"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Directed resistance to the counterattack and threatened McDowell’s right flank"}]]}],["$","div","Brigade",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Brigade"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Robert Trabue"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Four cohesive regiments facing McDowell with elements of other brigades"}]]}],["$","div","Brigades",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Brigades"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Preston Smith / Patton Anderson"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Opposed Marsh in a prolonged standoff"}]]}]]]}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"subsection-title","children":"Other people heard or discussed"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"people-grid compact-people","children":[["$","article","William T. Sherman",{"className":"person-card","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/william-t-sherman.jpg","alt":"Portrait of William T. Sherman","width":420,"height":520,"loading":"lazy"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"side union","children":"United States"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"William T. Sherman"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Proposed and directed the first substantial United States counterattack of the day"}]]}]]}],["$","article","John A. McClernand",{"className":"person-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"portrait-placeholder","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"JA"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"side union","children":"United States"}],["$","h3",null,{"